28rm|n|The act of varying; a partial change in the form, position, state, or qualities of a thing; modification; alternation; mutation; diversity; deviation; as, a variation of color in different lights; a variation in size; variation of language. ; Extent to which a thing varies; amount of departure from a position or state; amount or rate of change. ; Change of termination of words, as in declension, conjugation, derivation, etc. ; Repetition of a theme or melody with fanciful embellishments or modifications, in time, tune, or harmony, or sometimes change of key; the presentation of a musical thought in new and varied aspects, yet so that the essential features of the original shall still preserve their identity. ; One of the different arrangements which can be made of any number of quantities taking a certain number of them together.	a:2aw8,79,11;ko5,78,4;1x33,71,5;168q,37,3;1cca,34,12;1x8n,25,2;1xt5,23,12~1cca,34,12;1xt5,23,12;2aw8,79,11;1x33,71,5;ko5,78,4;168q,37,3;1x8n,25,2	V:1j5c,86,4~1j5c,86,4	n:2323,46,17~2323,46,17	N:w2,41,2~w2,41,2
